  "source": {
    "title": "Northern Whig, 13 January 1923, p. 6 (\"Ballyclare\"); Larne Times, 27 January 1923, p. 3 (\"Ballyclare Urban Council: annual meeting\")",
    "publisher": "Northern Whig (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "nominations as printed: 'There are nine seats in Ballyclare Council. The returning officer has received nominations on behalf of eight candidates—namely, Saml. Coleman, chairman of the last Council; Samuel Douther, retiring member; W. W. Boyd, John Forsythe, John Grange, Nathaniel M'Kinstry, Samuel M'Knight, and Houston Service. There were no withdrawals, and only one seat remains to be filled.'",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0007615/19230113/103/0006",
