    ]
  },
  "note": "Election of the Ballyclare Urban Council, January 1923. The council had nine seats; eight candidates were nominated for them, there were no withdrawals, and one seat remained to be filled (Northern Whig, 13 January 1923, p. 6). No poll; eight returned unopposed and the ninth seat was filled by co-opting William Kennedy at the annual meeting (Larne Times, 27 January 1923, p. 3). Returned unopposed."
